## Active license: Elastic License 2.0 (ELv2)

From commit `9798cf8` (2026-10-26) onward, this repository is licensed under the **Elastic License 2.0**. See [LICENSE](./LICENSE) for the full text. Licensor: Hsukqi Lee / Mythicove <team@tsinbei.com>.

## Historical license: AGPL-3.0

All commits up to and including `f9f41f5` were released under the **GNU Affero General Public License v3.0**, including the release tags:

- `v0.1.0` (2026-10-23)
- `v0.2.0` (2026-10-24)

AGPL-3.0 grants for those versions are irrevocable: anyone who received them before the relicense may continue to use and distribute those snapshots under AGPL-3.0 forever.

## Why the change

See [ADR-0004 (license policy)](https://docs.gov.skin/architecture/adr-0004-license/), revised 2026-10-24. In short:

- The project's intent is to prevent third parties from running it as a commercial hosted service — not to force derivatives open source. AGPL's copyleft raised the barrier for launcher/plugin/self-hosting ecosystem integration.
- ELv2's three restrictions match that intent exactly: no offering the software as a managed service to third parties, no circumventing license keys, no removing notices. Everything else (self-hosting, internal use, modification, client integration) remains free.
- The project has a single author and no external contributors, so the relicense applies unilaterally — and only to versions released after the relicense commit.

## What this means in practice

| Scenario | Result |
|---|---|
| Forked the repo before 2026-10-26 | Your snapshot stays AGPL-3.0 forever; code synced from upstream after the relicense carries ELv2. |
| Self-hosting, modification, building on it, client integration | Permitted under ELv2. |
| Offering it as a managed or hosted service to third parties | Not permitted under ELv2; a separate commercial license is required — contact <team@tsinbei.com>. |

